+another type such as :class:`pathlib.Path` with ``path_type``.
+
+Filenames are not always valid Unicode.  On such systems, Python represents
+the invalid bytes as surrogate escapes, which can still be used to open the
+file but may fail when printed.  Use :func:`format_filename` to display a
